User reported Podman refusing runner removal while nine agent-created containers referenced its network namespace, and requested preserving installed tools instead of automatic container replacement. The change keeps the retained image/process on image updates, rejects incompatible configuration before stopping, adds a confirmed idle rebuild action, and checks dependent containers before deletion. Validation: 24 Docker manager tests, 60 native worker tests, 12 Agent route tests, two real Podman integration tests, four Chromium checks (including mobile), frontend checks/build, all-target Clippy and rustfmt. Explicit stops and crash recovery retain their prior semantics; namespace-independent services are needed to survive those boundaries. No production containers were changed.
